      "message": "Yes, it\u0027s intentional: if a test hangs, a t.Fatal message is almost never helpful in diagnosing it.\n\nGiven the amount of concurrency in this package and the sheer number of different mutexes involved, I believe the most likely timing failure here is a deadlock or livelock involving lock-inversion and/or timers, in which case a goroutine dump is likely to be much more helpful — and a goroutine dump is exactly what we get if we simply allow the test to time out.",
